---
/** For people comfortable with servers: everything they need to run Little Dipper anywhere, today. */
---
<aside class="band" style="padding: 24px 28px; margin-top: 22px">
  <div class="kicker">For the technically comfortable</div>
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; margin-top: 4px">Run it anywhere today</h3>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 10px">Little Dipper is a ready-made Docker image:</p>
  <p style="margin: 0 0 12px"><code style="font-size: 15px">ghcr.io/big-dipper/littledipper:latest</code></p>
  <ul class="prose" style="margin: 0">
    <li>Works on Intel and ARM machines, including a Raspberry Pi or Apple Silicon.</li>
    <li>It needs four things: port 4000 behind HTTPS, a persistent disk at <code>/data</code>, <code>LD_PUBLIC_URL</code> set to its address, and a passkey-capable browser to claim it.</li>
    <li>The claim link is in its logs when it first starts.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note" style="margin: 12px 0 0">Everything else is in the <a href="https://github.com/big-dipper/littledipper#deploy">Little Dipper README</a>. Each release has its own version tag if you’d rather pick when to update.</p>
</aside>
